    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Hunt Prey",
      "actions": 1,
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "concentrate"
      ],
      "text": "The Isgeri Slayer designates a single creature they can see and hear, or one they're Tracking, as their prey.\n\nThe slayer gains a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks to seek the prey and to Survival checks to track the prey.\n\nThe first time the slayer hits the designated prey in a round, they deal an additional 1d8 precision damage. The slayer also ignores the penalty for making ranged attacks within their second range increment. These effects last until the poacher uses Hunt Prey again.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "key": "roll-option",
          "option": "hunted-prey",
          "toggleable": true,
          "label": "PF2E.SpecificRule.HuntPrey.TargetHuntedPrey"
        },
        {
          "key": "modifier",
          "selector": "perception",
          "type": "circumstance",
          "value": 2,
          "when": [
            "action:seek",
            "hunted-prey"
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "modifier",
          "selector": "survival",
          "type": "circumstance",
          "value": 2,
          "when": [
            "action:track",
            "hunted-prey"
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "roll-option",
          "option": "ignore-range-penalty:2",
          "domain": "ranged-attack-roll",
          "when": [
            "hunted-prey"
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "roll-option",
          "option": "first-attack",
          "toggleable": true,
          "label": "PF2E.SpecificRule.Ranger.HuntersEdge.FirstAttack"
        },
        {
          "key": "damage-dice",
          "selector": "strike-damage",
          "dice": 1,
          "die": "d8",
          "category": "precision",
          "when": [
            "first-attack"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Twin Takedown",
      "actions": 1,
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "flourish"
      ],
      "text": "Requirements The Isgeri Slayer is wielding two melee weapons, each in a different hand\n\n---\nEffect The Isgeri Slayer swiftly attacks their hunted prey with each of their weapons, potentially combining their damage into a single devastating attack. They make two Strikes against their hunted prey, one with each of the required weapons. If both hit the same hunted prey, combine their damage for the purpose of its resistances and weaknesses. The Isgeri Slayer applies their multiple attack penalty to each Strike normally."
    }
  ],
